  "live_records": {
    "q-183319": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183319",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$ \n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cup (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
