    "q-183351": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183351",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $x$ is a multiple of $10,$ then $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $10.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x$ is not is a multiple of $10.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not a multiple of $10,$ or $x$ is a multiple of $5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
