    "q-183380": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183380",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14271133/assets/20783ac512f10184d50d2069792fdf42e701667125b07179236a8b0524b684b2.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14271133/assets/0188e215f62afde3fa730642703fb6e2b213f8864f912ac0688d35fa29bb4db2.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14271133/assets/f4df9eb071e2deb4c79c8928a7b9e60f3341bba827a5fbb328e864d2de9a5803.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14271133/assets/f17a4b0599a2dcc3d83d455c9be4e8a5033b7175c1859bfa634d2a3367553e0a.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14271133/assets/4683bc52b9d18e7710b593d36ca191adeee6ecbc93428e1f40dd7161794090d8.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-183380-a",
              "type": "image",
